<article class="env-lemma" id="069E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/069E">Lemma <span data-tag="069E">37.62.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $U$, $P$, $P'$ be schemes over $S$. Let $u \in U$. Let $i : U \to P$, $i' : U \to P'$ be immersions over $S$. Assume $P$ and $P'$ smooth over $S$. Then the following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$i$ is a Koszul-regular immersion in a neighbourhood of $u$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$i'$ is a Koszul-regular immersion in a neighbourhood of $u$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $i$ is a Koszul-regular immersion in a neighbourhood of $u$. Consider the morphism $j = (i, i') : U \to P \times _ S P' = P''$. Since $P'' = P \times _ S P' \to P$ is smooth, it follows from Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/067S" data-tag="067S">31.23.9</a> that $j$ is a Koszul-regular immersion, whereupon it follows from Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0693" data-tag="0693">31.23.12</a> that $i'$ is a Koszul-regular immersion. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>